# Every file here is text, and every working copy should hold the same bytes, on
# whichever operating system it was cloned onto. Without this line, Git on Windows
# checks these files out with CRLF line endings instead of the LF they were written
# with. That is harmless for Node - but this repo exists to argue that identical
# bytes hash to identical fingerprints, so it would be a strange place to let a
# checkout quietly rewrite bytes.
#
# To be clear about what was never at risk: nothing the five programs produce
# passes through Git. Exports, sidecars and proofs are generated on your machine
# and ignored by the file next to this one, so no hash and no proof ever depended
# on Git's line-ending choices. This is only about the source you clone matching
# the source that was tested.
* text=auto eol=lf
